    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The release note alone [ev-44e4f5150126] is vague, but the linked PR fills the gap. [ev-da751251ff93] and [ev-49706aa0f16b] say the settings code used to hand out a pointer to the argocd-cm ConfigMap (and to secrets) held in the shared informer cache, which several threads used and could change. That caused a data race seen in tests. The fix returns a deep copy instead, at a slight performance cost. [ev-b7039b930620] shows the change is limited to internal code (util/settings and util/db), with no config key, flag or default changed. That is enough to write the assertion: the subject is Argo CD's internal settings/ConfigMap access, the change is a behaviour change to return copies, it applies to every installation, and the consequence is informational (a race is removed, a small performance cost is added, and operators need do nothing).",
